    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d133-a7">

                <pb facs="0282" n="226" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg226"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 6 in No. 76.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Lord Derby to Mr. Hoffman</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-05-03"><hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 3,
                        1876</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my letter of yesterday’s
                    date, I have the honor to inform you that an application was made this morning
                    before Baron Pollock by Winslow’s solicitor for his release, but that, on a
                    statement from Her Majesty’s attorney-general that negotiations ou the subject
                    were going on between Her Majesty’s government and the United States Government,
                    the judge remanded the case for ten days.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>DERBY.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
